/P 66 0 R
/E (Can I Hinder? is a crowd- interactive game built as a distributed system, Instead of it being a single application it is made up of several connected components, each responsible for a different part of the experience.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (At its core, the system combines a real-time C++ game client with web technologies that allow spectators to interact with gameplay as it happens. These interactions are handled through a WebSocket relay server, supported by a REST API for authentication and a Progressive Web App \(PWA\) for user interaction.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
